cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite this record and the SIR method paper (see preferred-citation)."
type: dataset
title: "SIR per-unit synergy test results for DrugCombDB (O'Neil and NCI-ALMANAC)"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/AsiaeeLab/isosynergy"
keywords:
  - drug combinations
  - drug synergy
  - Bliss independence
  - isotonic regression
  - DrugCombDB
  - NCI-ALMANAC
  - hypothesis testing
abstract: >
  Per-unit results of the SIR test against Bliss independence for 23,052 O'Neil
  units and 227,323 NCI-ALMANAC plates in DrugCombDB: activity, mean Bliss excess
  with standard error and companion p-value, the SIR statistic with its p-value,
  q-values within declared testing families, region-scan results, fragility
  diagnostics, the data-handling log and the seed of every fit. No binary
  synergy labels are included.
